WEBVTT

00:09.070 --> 00:13.080
She lives in a different time and space than we do.

00:13.080 --> 00:16.160
Her thoughts are always a mystery.

00:16.160 --> 00:18.410
It makes her difficult to babysit.

00:19.170 --> 00:24.300
But she is needed, Gido.

00:24.550 --> 00:28.260
Yes, I will bring her back.

00:29.340 --> 00:30.390
I'm counting on you.

00:31.180 --> 00:33.760
We're running out of time.

00:37.980 --> 00:39.770
Bainas, I'm coming in.

00:39.770 --> 00:40.770
Sure.

00:45.020 --> 00:45.940
What's this?

00:48.070 --> 00:50.660
It's the chart for that girl Sam brought in.

00:53.240 --> 00:56.580
I noticed something odd when I was treating her,
so I took a closer look...

00:58.290 --> 00:59.500
What?

00:59.910 --> 01:01.210
She's no ordinary person...

01:02.380 --> 01:03.500
That girl.

01:11.630 --> 01:11.680
LEIJI MATSUMOTO'S

01:11.630 --> 01:11.680
OZMA

01:17.640 --> 01:20.600
You looked over the desert wasteland from above

01:20.600 --> 01:23.810
kareki wo sora de mioroshita

01:20.600 --> 01:23.810
and saw dead trees scattered throughout

01:23.810 --> 01:29.490
aoi tori ga nageki naku to

01:23.810 --> 01:29.490
Blue bird, who knows no sadness

01:30.070 --> 01:32.990
machigai darake no kibou no

01:30.070 --> 01:32.990
I ground my teeth, my hope full of misconceptions

01:32.990 --> 01:37.950
okuba de kanda nigai suna hakidasenai

01:32.990 --> 01:37.950
and couldn't spit out the dreadful sand in my mouth

01:37.950 --> 01:43.080
atoaji wa namida he to toketa

01:37.950 --> 01:43.080
Left was only the salt of tears

01:43.080 --> 01:48.500
aisuru mono sae mamorenai okubyou mono ni

01:43.080 --> 01:48.500
For cowards unable to protect the ones they love

01:48.500 --> 01:54.260
michitarita asa wa konai

01:48.500 --> 01:54.260
no future waits past the dawn of day

01:54.640 --> 01:55.430
Woah

01:55.010 --> 01:55.760
oh

01:55.430 --> 01:56.260
oh!

01:55.800 --> 02:00.730
asu no tobira doko he tsuzuitemo

01:55.800 --> 02:00.730
Wherever the door to the future may lead

02:00.730 --> 02:05.940
haruka misueta me wa nidoto sorasanai

02:00.730 --> 02:05.940
I'll stay focused on what I need to do for it myself

02:05.940 --> 02:07.400
Oh,

02:07.020 --> 02:07.820
woah

02:07.360 --> 02:08.270
oh

02:07.820 --> 02:08.610
oh!

02:08.190 --> 02:12.990
itoshiki kimi no kokoro tataku yo

02:08.190 --> 02:12.990
I will take my place in your heart

02:12.990 --> 02:22.250
itsuka tadashii sekai he kimi wo tsureteyuku kara

02:12.990 --> 02:22.250
because one day I will show you the world we should live in

02:37.510 --> 02:43.020
Episode 3: A Thousand Years of Doubt

02:51.440 --> 02:54.450
We call this place the shelter.

02:55.030 --> 02:56.280
The shelter?

02:56.280 --> 02:57.030
Yup.

02:57.990 --> 03:00.540
This lagoon's surrounded by rocks.

03:00.540 --> 03:03.040
To get in,
you gotta go underground.

03:03.410 --> 03:08.330
A long time ago,
people turned this place into a sanctuary.

03:22.180 --> 03:24.560
<i>It's about that girl Sam brought in.</i>

03:25.060 --> 03:26.440
You mean Maya?

03:26.440 --> 03:29.020
I noticed something when I was treating her.

03:29.020 --> 03:30.230
Something strange.

03:30.770 --> 03:31.730
Strange?

03:32.020 --> 03:41.700
You're aware that Theseus is composed of
designer clones called "Ideal Children", yes?

03:41.700 --> 03:42.740
Yes.

03:43.160 --> 03:46.500
Well, this one is different.

03:46.750 --> 03:49.000
She's physically closer to us Natura.

03:49.710 --> 03:51.250
What does that mean?

03:54.300 --> 03:56.170
I've seen this before.

03:56.170 --> 03:58.840
Something similar happened once in the past,

03:58.840 --> 04:02.140
where a wounded Theseus soldier
I was treating

04:02.510 --> 04:04.970
turned out to be a Natura clone.

04:06.480 --> 04:09.230
There's only one conclusion
I can draw from this.

04:09.230 --> 04:14.780
It's possible that
the Ideal Children's clone bodies

04:14.780 --> 04:19.490
have degraded over
many generations of copying,

04:19.700 --> 04:25.240
and they've started using
Natura bodies to survive.

04:27.290 --> 04:29.870
Could it be that she's...

04:33.420 --> 04:36.550
She's no ordinary person.

04:58.240 --> 04:59.570
Check it out!

05:09.080 --> 05:12.000
This place is full of old machines.

05:12.000 --> 05:17.380
Here's where we found my Fluke Fish,
and the engine that lets us dive.

05:18.880 --> 05:20.550
Does this run?

05:24.850 --> 05:27.770
Yeah, I keep her tickin'.

05:27.770 --> 05:29.390
She's good to go anytime.

05:34.310 --> 05:35.730
See?

05:37.360 --> 05:39.820
Could I pilot it?

05:39.820 --> 05:40.900
Sure.

05:40.900 --> 05:43.570
I'll show you the ropes
when you're feeling a bit better.

05:46.330 --> 05:49.700
But don't you worry 'bout that!
Check out the main attraction!

05:54.880 --> 05:56.630
Up here!

05:56.630 --> 05:59.010
Whatcha think? Surprised?

05:59.010 --> 06:03.630
You could say this is kinda like the
opposite of a quantum transition engine.

06:04.340 --> 06:09.640
Fire this Monokeros into a QTF,
and it'll stop the whole thing dead.

06:11.180 --> 06:12.310
Well?

06:12.310 --> 06:13.480
Amazing, huh?

06:16.770 --> 06:19.030
I guess that kinda went over your head.

06:19.030 --> 06:22.240
So... basically...

06:23.450 --> 06:25.200
Once this thing's complete,

06:25.200 --> 06:30.080
I can use it to trap that sand whale,
Ozma, under the ground.

06:30.080 --> 06:31.750
Piece of cake!

06:37.130 --> 06:40.460
Why are you chasing the Ozma?

06:41.550 --> 06:44.090
My brother was the one
who got this thing up and running,

06:44.510 --> 06:46.970
along with the quantum transition engine.

06:48.430 --> 06:49.760
But...

06:49.760 --> 06:52.890
He went missing one day
while chasing the Ozma.

06:53.850 --> 06:55.980
If only the Monokeros had been ready...

06:57.020 --> 06:59.320
My brother was freakin' awesome!

06:59.320 --> 07:02.280
Way better than I'll ever be.

07:05.610 --> 07:09.830
But, if I can use this thing
to bring down Ozma,

07:10.700 --> 07:13.410
I'll be that little bit closer
to following in his footsteps.

07:24.050 --> 07:25.300
Captain?

07:26.630 --> 07:27.640
Sam.

07:27.640 --> 07:29.930
Get back to the ship.

07:29.930 --> 07:32.060
I want to talk to Maya.

07:32.060 --> 07:33.770
Y-Yes, ma'am.

07:40.060 --> 07:43.070
Maya, what are you?

07:46.570 --> 07:52.450
The rumor is that you're like a queen to Theseus.

07:52.450 --> 07:57.830
So why did you take off in a yacht and run away?

07:59.710 --> 08:04.090
I... can't stay here.

08:06.090 --> 08:09.140
The Theseus military is searching for me.

08:09.140 --> 08:12.100
It won't be long before they find me here.

08:12.350 --> 08:15.100
I don't want to put you in danger again!

08:15.100 --> 08:18.600
You didn't answer my question.

08:20.810 --> 08:23.110
I don't know anymore.

08:23.940 --> 08:27.360
The creature that you know
as the sand whale, Ozma...

08:27.360 --> 08:30.240
I came here to meet it.

08:31.620 --> 08:33.990
Ozma? What do you mean?

08:35.410 --> 08:39.120
Even if I wanted to answer you, I couldn't.

08:40.620 --> 08:42.500
I feel like I've been lost a long time,

08:43.380 --> 08:46.550
maybe even a thousand years,

08:47.300 --> 08:50.050
searching for that answer.

08:52.510 --> 08:55.770
I... I...

08:55.770 --> 08:57.180
Maya!

08:58.180 --> 08:59.060
Are you okay?

08:59.520 --> 09:02.400
Maya's tired, Captain!

09:02.810 --> 09:04.190
Do what you want.

09:04.480 --> 09:07.400
First, you gotta get better. Okay?

09:07.400 --> 09:08.650
Let's get back to the ship.

09:31.840 --> 09:32.590
Oww...

09:32.590 --> 09:35.010
What were you doing in the doorway?

09:35.010 --> 09:37.260
Does it matter? How is she?

09:37.260 --> 09:38.430
She's okay, right?

09:38.430 --> 09:40.850
The doctor is still examining her.

09:40.850 --> 09:43.480
These things take time! You know that!

09:57.950 --> 09:59.330
Why?

09:59.330 --> 10:03.620
She looks like she's still
in her teens or early twenties...

10:03.620 --> 10:06.710
Why are her telomeres so short?

10:15.720 --> 10:18.390
I'm makin' extra today, guys!

10:18.390 --> 10:20.720
Dig in!

10:22.230 --> 10:23.730
I'm gonna eat like a pig today!

10:23.730 --> 10:26.730
Yeah! We came back
from the edge of hell, after all!

10:26.730 --> 10:30.360
I'm gonna eat, and eat,
and eat until I can see heaven!

10:32.700 --> 10:35.700
Man, that was close yesterday.

10:35.700 --> 10:38.830
Yeah. We were almost boiled alive.

10:38.830 --> 10:42.500
Why was Theseus following us, anyway?

10:42.750 --> 10:47.250
I heard it's because of that girl the kid brought in.

10:47.590 --> 10:51.260
She brought bad luck to the Bardanos.

10:51.260 --> 10:52.670
Hey, hold it right there!

10:52.670 --> 10:54.180
The hell you think you're talkin' about, Souryuu?

10:54.180 --> 10:56.430
You know damn well what I'm talkin' about!

10:56.430 --> 10:58.260
Everyone here knows!

10:58.260 --> 11:01.470
That girl you brought here
is some kinda freaky witch-

11:01.470 --> 11:02.730
You shut the hell-

11:03.810 --> 11:04.980
H-Hey!

11:04.980 --> 11:05.730
Lemme go!

11:05.730 --> 11:09.110
What's wrong? That all you got, kid?

11:06.900 --> 11:08.230
I said, lemme go!

11:09.110 --> 11:10.480
Sam's in trouble.

11:10.480 --> 11:12.990
Guess we'd better help him, right?

11:12.990 --> 11:14.610
Get 'em!

11:30.090 --> 11:31.710
What the hell d'you think you're doin'?!

11:31.710 --> 11:34.260
We haven't had this much food in ages!

11:34.590 --> 11:36.010
Boys!

11:36.010 --> 11:37.890
Get in there!

11:37.890 --> 11:39.890
Right away, chief!

11:42.390 --> 11:43.600
This looks fun.

11:43.600 --> 11:45.310
Wanna get a piece of the action?

11:45.310 --> 11:46.390
Hell yeah!

11:47.020 --> 11:49.020
No thanks.

11:49.900 --> 11:51.440
I'm too busy eating.

11:52.400 --> 11:54.570
Aw, you're no fun!

11:54.820 --> 11:56.450
I finished the washing.

11:56.450 --> 11:57.860
Mimay!

11:57.860 --> 11:59.490
Mimay, have you seen her?

11:59.490 --> 12:01.030
Wh-What's wrong?

12:01.030 --> 12:04.250
I took my eyes off her for one second
and she vanished into thin air!

12:11.420 --> 12:13.420
Avast, ye useless lubbers!

12:16.590 --> 12:20.050
Sam! Maya ran away
from the infirmary and is now missing.

12:21.180 --> 12:23.810
We can't find her anywhere on the ship!

12:25.350 --> 12:27.850
Could I pilot it?

12:27.850 --> 12:28.730
Sure.

12:28.730 --> 12:31.400
I'll show you the ropes
when you're feeling a bit better.

12:32.440 --> 12:33.860
She must be there!

12:33.860 --> 12:35.320
Where are you going?

12:35.320 --> 12:37.820
Maya was interested in one of the small ships.

12:37.990 --> 12:39.820
But where would she even find a ship like that?

12:39.820 --> 12:41.820
There are dozens in the shelter!

12:42.200 --> 12:43.410
Stop her!

12:43.410 --> 12:44.450
Right!

13:17.030 --> 13:18.820
Wait! Stop!

13:19.320 --> 13:22.820
She's gonna cross the atoll
and head for the desert!

13:27.410 --> 13:29.410
I'll bring her back!

13:29.660 --> 13:30.910
I'm counting on you!

13:38.170 --> 13:39.550
Damn it!

13:44.300 --> 13:46.930
Why are you trying to run away from us?

13:49.430 --> 13:50.390
There she is!

13:54.650 --> 13:56.270
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

13:56.270 --> 14:03.450
<i>But... I don't know
what's right and wrong anymore...</i>

14:09.660 --> 14:11.290
Silence.

14:12.460 --> 14:15.670
We will now ask the Diet for their vote.

14:26.010 --> 14:28.810
The vote is decided in favor.

14:37.820 --> 14:41.110
Silence! Silence!

14:41.360 --> 14:43.610
We don't have a choice.

14:43.610 --> 14:48.580
If we are to survive
as this planet's continued rulers...

15:01.090 --> 15:03.630
How strong...

15:03.970 --> 15:08.180
I take it that this is the one, Mr. Gido?

15:37.120 --> 15:42.800
We Ideal Children
are those with the best possible DNA.

15:43.670 --> 15:46.260
That is why we exist.

15:48.300 --> 15:54.520
Perhaps the fatal flaw of science is
that it strips mankind of its dignity.

16:12.410 --> 16:13.290
<i>Zone...</i>

16:14.580 --> 16:16.080
<i>If I could get there,</i>

16:16.790 --> 16:18.580
<i>the future would change...</i>

16:19.580 --> 16:24.250
<i>I may learn something by meeting you...</i>

16:25.960 --> 16:26.920
<i>Ozma...</i>

16:29.470 --> 16:30.840
Maya!

16:31.850 --> 16:32.850
Hey!

16:33.970 --> 16:35.180
Wait!

16:37.180 --> 16:38.390
Let's go back to the ship.

16:38.890 --> 16:41.690
There's no way you're gonna
cross the desert in that state!

16:41.690 --> 16:43.610
Please, let me go!

16:43.610 --> 16:45.820
Let you go where?

16:46.110 --> 16:47.820
You don't need to run away.

16:47.820 --> 16:49.860
Everyone at Bardanos will look out for you!

16:50.110 --> 16:51.870
They're family.

16:51.870 --> 16:54.120
It's our home!

16:56.620 --> 16:57.580
Thank you.

16:58.750 --> 17:02.750
But that's why I don't want you
to be in danger anymore!

17:06.420 --> 17:07.510
This is...

17:07.920 --> 17:08.920
It can't be Ozma?

17:08.920 --> 17:09.930
No!

17:14.600 --> 17:16.180
We gotta get away from here!

17:36.620 --> 17:37.620
Maya...

17:38.370 --> 17:39.620
Don't let go!

17:49.300 --> 17:51.010
Maya!

18:01.480 --> 18:02.480
Maya!

18:12.610 --> 18:15.870
Captain, shall we take the Natura boy as well?

18:18.490 --> 18:19.490
Sam!

18:19.750 --> 18:20.500
Maya!

18:21.500 --> 18:23.250
There's no need.

18:23.710 --> 18:24.920
Prepare to fire.

18:24.920 --> 18:26.250
No!

18:26.250 --> 18:27.500
Stop!

18:27.500 --> 18:28.590
Miss Maya...

18:31.880 --> 18:33.010
This is an order.

18:33.550 --> 18:36.260
That boy saved my life.

18:36.550 --> 18:39.640
I will not allow you to hurt him.

18:39.640 --> 18:41.890
Give Maya back, you masked freak!

18:42.060 --> 18:44.270
Give her back or you're gonna regret it!

18:44.730 --> 18:47.270
Get Miss Maya back in the ship.

18:48.270 --> 18:50.780
Please, Gido! Don't!

18:51.150 --> 18:51.780
Gido!

18:53.990 --> 18:55.030
Maya!

18:57.240 --> 18:58.410
Please...

18:58.990 --> 18:59.790
Please.

19:00.580 --> 19:01.580
Save him.

19:02.660 --> 19:04.580
Ozma!

19:07.750 --> 19:09.090
Captain!

19:09.290 --> 19:13.630
We're seeing a massive quasi-transition
field 2000 meters off the bow!

19:13.630 --> 19:15.340
Is it the sand pirates' ship?

19:15.340 --> 19:16.220
No.

19:16.220 --> 19:17.970
It's too big.

19:17.970 --> 19:18.890
It's probably...

19:27.690 --> 19:28.520
Ozma...

19:28.520 --> 19:29.900
Emergency dive!

19:31.530 --> 19:33.530
Sam! Sam!

19:33.900 --> 19:35.030
Maya!

19:35.240 --> 19:37.780
Get Miss Maya inside the ship, now!

19:40.530 --> 19:42.040
Get out of here, Sam!

19:42.450 --> 19:44.080
Run!

19:46.250 --> 19:47.750
Wait!

20:25.790 --> 20:26.870
Ozma...

21:07.250 --> 21:08.410
Sam!

21:08.620 --> 21:10.080
Are you okay?

21:19.590 --> 21:21.340
Looks like he's still in one piece.

21:21.340 --> 21:23.930
He's got better luck than his brother, at least.

21:30.100 --> 21:36.530
shin'ai naru anata he

21:30.100 --> 21:36.530
I ask you, my love,

21:36.530 --> 21:43.910
since when your heart

21:42.910 --> 21:49.500
setsunasa to kodoku no aida

21:42.910 --> 21:49.500
has been lost between sorrow and solitude

21:49.500 --> 21:56.000
hasamarete kokyuu wo wasureteru

21:49.500 --> 21:56.000
where you lost your grip on reality

21:56.000 --> 22:02.510
kanashii uta ni tsutsumarete

21:56.000 --> 22:02.510
All around us we hear songs of lament

22:02.510 --> 22:09.020
namida ga ochiru sono mae ni

22:02.510 --> 22:09.020
but before I give in to the tears

22:08.010 --> 22:14.650
kizuite anata wo omoinagara

22:08.010 --> 22:14.650
I notice the echoes

22:14.650 --> 22:23.610
yasashiku hibiku utagoe ni

22:14.650 --> 22:23.610
of a gentle singing voice around me

22:23.860 --> 22:31.540
dareka wo aishite dareka ni aisare

22:23.860 --> 22:31.540
Loving someone and being loved by someone

22:30.540 --> 22:36.880
umareta imi ni sotto kizuketa nara

22:30.540 --> 22:36.880
is why we were all born

22:36.880 --> 22:44.380
omoi no mama ni koe wo furishibotte

22:36.880 --> 22:43.170
If you realized that too, put your emotions

22:42.170 --> 22:44.380
into your voice

22:44.380 --> 22:54.520
anata mo tsuyoku ai wo utatte hoshii

22:44.380 --> 22:54.520
and please sing of love with all your strength

22:59.940 --> 23:11.950
Next Episode

23:00.940 --> 23:03.360
Sam's planning on bringing Maya back himself.

23:03.360 --> 23:04.950
Mimay went with him.

23:04.950 --> 23:08.070
But that's one of Theseus's
newest subterranean craft.

23:08.070 --> 23:09.490
Then let's get going, too!

23:09.490 --> 23:13.410
Captain, let's have an all-out
duel under the sand!

23:11.950 --> 23:14.960
Episode 4: To the Ends of the Earth
